  "body": "## Problem\nThe anonymous market observer now starts correctly and reaches target filtering, but the latest runtime log shows Vinted's OneTrust preference-center overlay physically intercepting clicks on `catalog--catalog-filter--trigger` for the full 30-second Playwright click timeout. The blocker is specifically `.onetrust-pc-dark-filter` / `#onetrust-policy-text`, so the observer fails the first exact VINTED_MODEL target before any market scan can be recorded.\n\n## Changes\n- add a narrow browser-context OneTrust guard for every Playwright context\n- handle both the normal banner accept control and OneTrust preference-center `accept-recommended` control\n- match only exact known accept-all labels inside OneTrust DOM\n- if the preference center itself is blocking the page and no accept-all control is available, use OneTrust's own save/close control instead of deleting/force-clicking DOM\n- combine MutationObserver with a short bounded poll because OneTrust may attach handlers/open its preference center without a useful DOM mutation\n- keep the existing anonymous-observer UI guard and exact model/category fail-closed checks unchanged\n- add unit coverage for the exact OneTrust controls and absence of broad page-wide button clicking\n\n## Safety\n- no negotiation, real-action, quota or target-matching semantics change\n- no arbitrary modal dismissal\n- no DOM overlay removal or force-click through blockers\n- normal logged-in bots remain compatible; their existing LoginService cookie handling is simply backed by the same narrowly scoped guard",
